\section{Relativistic Particle Dynamics}
The motion of a charged particle under electromagnetic fields is governed by the relativistic Lorentz force:
\begin{equation}
\frac{d\mathbf{p}}{dt} = q\left( \mathbf{E} + \mathbf{v} \times \mathbf{B} \right),
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{p} = \gamma m \mathbf{v}$ and $\gamma = (1 - v^2/c^2)^{-1/2}$.

\subsection{Relativistic Boris Integrator}
The Boris method is widely used in particle-in-cell (PIC) simulations due to its excellent long-term stability and energy behavior. 
SIE-ASTRO implements the relativistic variant:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Half-step electric acceleration:
    \[
    \mathbf{u}^{-} = \gamma\mathbf{v} + \frac{q\Delta t}{2m}\mathbf{E}.
    \]
    \item Rotation due to magnetic field:
    \[
    \mathbf{u}' = \mathbf{u}^{-} + \mathbf{u}^{-} \times \mathbf{t},
    \]
    where
    \[
    \mathbf{t} = \frac{q\Delta t}{2m\gamma'}\mathbf{B}.
    \]
    \item Final half-step electric acceleration:
    \[
    \mathbf{u}^{+} = \mathbf{u}' + \mathbf{u}' \times \mathbf{s},
    \]
    with
    \[
    \mathbf{s} = \frac{2\mathbf{t}}{1 + t^2}.
    \]
\end{enumerate}

The updated velocity is:
\[
\mathbf{v}_{n+1} = \frac{\mathbf{u}^{+}}{\gamma_{\text{new}}}.
\]

\section{Maxwell Solver: Constrained Transport}
The electromagnetic fields evolve according to Maxwell's equations. 
SIE-ASTRO uses a staggered Yee mesh and a constrained-transport (CT) update to preserve $\nabla\cdot\mathbf{B}=0$.

\subsection{Faraday Update}
The magnetic field update is:
\begin{equation}
\frac{\partial \mathbf{B}}{\partial t} = -\nabla \times \mathbf{E}.
\end{equation}

The discrete CT update ensures divergence-free evolution:
\[
B_x^{n+1} = B_x^n - \Delta t\left( 
\frac{E_z(i,j+1,k) - E_z(i,j,k)}{\Delta y}
-
\frac{E_y(i,j,k+1) - E_y(i,j,k)}{\Delta z}
\right),
\]
with analogous expressions for $B_y$ and $B_z$.

\section{Software Architecture}
The engine is organized into three core modules:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \texttt{Particles.hpp}: Relativistic particle system and Boris integrator.
    \item \texttt{GridFields.hpp}: Yee grid and constrained-transport Maxwell solver.
    \item \texttt{CryptoPipeline.hpp}: AES-256-GCM encryption pipeline.
\end{enumerate}

The main driver executes:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Field update,
    \item Particle push,
    \item Diagnostic encryption every 250 steps.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Cryptographic Ingestion Pipeline}
Diagnostics are encrypted using AES-256-GCM:
\begin{itemize}
    \item 32-byte key,
    \item 12-byte IV,
    \item 16-byte authentication tag.
\end{itemize}

